3. CRUD OPERATIONS (INSERT, SELECT, UPDATE, DELETE)
================================================================================
Every screen in Zaika performs four basic database actions:

A. CREATE (`INSERT INTO`) — Adding Tables & Menu Dishes:
```sql
INSERT INTO restaurant_tables (table_number, capacity, qr_token) VALUES
('T1', 2, 'tok_t1_99a1'),
('T2', 4, 'tok_t2_88b2'),
('T3', 4, 'tok_t3_77c3');

INSERT INTO menu_items (name, category, kitchen_station, price_half, price_full, is_veg, allergens, deal_badge, prep_time_mins)
VALUES
('Paneer Tikka', 'Main Course', 'Tandoor', 160.00, 260.00, TRUE, 'Dairy', 'Deal of the Day', 15),
('Butter Chicken', 'Main Course', 'Curry', 210.00, 340.00, FALSE, 'Dairy,Nuts', NULL, 18),
('Mango Lassi', 'Drinks', 'Drinks', NULL, 110.00, TRUE, 'Dairy', NULL, 5);
```

B. READ (`SELECT` with Filtering) — Customer QR Menu Search & Filters:
```sql
-- Fetch all available Veg dishes without Nuts, sorted by price
SELECT id, name, category, price_half, price_full, deal_badge
FROM menu_items
WHERE is_available = TRUE
  AND is_veg = TRUE
  AND (allergens IS NULL OR allergens NOT LIKE '%Nuts%')
ORDER BY price_full ASC;
```

C. UPDATE (`UPDATE ... SET`) — Moving Order Status & Table Floor Map:
```sql
-- Staff clicks "Send to Kitchen" on Order #1
UPDATE orders
SET status = 'Cooking',
    cooking_started_at = NOW(),
    estimated_ready_at = DATE_ADD(NOW(), INTERVAL 15 MINUTE)
WHERE id = 1;

-- Update Table T1 status on Live Floor Map
UPDATE restaurant_tables
SET status = 'Eating'
WHERE table_number = 'T1';
```

D. DELETE (`DELETE FROM`) — Owner Removes a Discontinued Dish:
```sql
DELETE FROM menu_items
WHERE id = 99;
```

