4. JOINS & AGGREGATIONS (KDS BOARD, BILLS & OWNER ANALYTICS)
================================================================================
Because data is split cleanly across normalized tables, `INNER JOIN` and `GROUP BY` combine them into live dashboards and itemized bills.

A. Kitchen Display System (KDS) Query — Fetch Active Items by Station:
```sql
SELECT
    o.id AS order_id,
    rt.table_number,
    mi.kitchen_station,
    mi.name AS dish_name,
    oi.portion_size,
    oi.spice_choice,
    oi.quantity,
    oi.item_status,
    TIMESTAMPDIFF(MINUTE, o.cooking_started_at, NOW()) AS elapsed_mins
FROM order_items oi
INNER JOIN orders o ON oi.order_id = o.id
INNER JOIN restaurant_tables rt ON o.table_id = rt.id
INNER JOIN menu_items mi ON oi.menu_item_id = mi.id
WHERE o.status IN ('Confirmed', 'Cooking')
  AND oi.item_status != 'Ready'
ORDER BY o.placed_at ASC;
```

B. Auto-Generate Itemized Table Bill (`SUM` & `GROUP BY`):
```sql
SELECT
    rt.table_number,
    SUM(oi.quantity * oi.unit_price) AS subtotal,
    ROUND(SUM(oi.quantity * oi.unit_price) * 0.05, 2) AS gst_5_percent,
    ROUND(SUM(oi.quantity * oi.unit_price) * 1.05, 2) AS total_with_gst
FROM orders o
INNER JOIN restaurant_tables rt ON o.table_id = rt.id
INNER JOIN order_items oi ON o.id = oi.order_id
WHERE rt.table_number = 'T1'
  AND o.status != 'Closed'
GROUP BY rt.table_number;
```

C. Owner Dashboard — Top-Selling Dishes & Waiter SLA Response Time:
```sql
-- Top 5 Best-Selling Dishes
SELECT
    mi.name AS dish_name,
    SUM(oi.quantity) AS total_sold,
    SUM(oi.quantity * oi.unit_price) AS revenue_generated
FROM order_items oi
INNER JOIN menu_items mi ON oi.menu_item_id = mi.id
GROUP BY mi.id, mi.name
ORDER BY total_sold DESC
LIMIT 5;

-- Average Call Waiter Response Speed (in seconds)
SELECT
    u.full_name AS waiter_name,
    COUNT(cwr.id) AS alerts_resolved,
    ROUND(AVG(cwr.response_seconds), 1) AS avg_response_sec
FROM call_waiter_requests cwr
INNER JOIN users u ON cwr.resolved_by = u.id
WHERE cwr.status = 'Resolved'
GROUP BY u.id, u.full_name;
```

