5. DATABASE NORMALIZATION (1NF, 2NF, 3NF) — INTERVIEW FAVORITE
================================================================================
Interviewers frequently ask how your database avoids duplicate data:
- 1NF (First Normal Form): Every cell holds a single atomic value (we never store `"2x Paneer Tikka, 1x Naan"` in one text column; each dish gets its own row in `order_items`).
- 2NF (Second Normal Form): Every non-key column depends on the entire Primary Key (dish details like `kitchen_station` and `allergens` live in `menu_items`, not repeated inside `order_items`).
- 3NF (Third Normal Form): No transitive dependencies (table `capacity` and `qr_token` live in `restaurant_tables`, referenced by `table_id` in `orders` and `bills`).
- Intentional Snapshot Exception: We store `unit_price` inside `order_items` so if the Owner raises Paneer Tikka's price tomorrow, yesterday's historical bills remain accurate!

